1
00:00:02,296 --> 00:00:04,816
So now with arrays out of the way, a very

2
00:00:04,849 --> 00:00:07,241
useful construct for managing lists of data,

3
00:00:07,482 --> 00:00:10,099
let's have a look at Sets because Sets are

4
00:00:10,452 --> 00:00:13,118
also about lists of data but they work a bit

5
00:00:13,118 --> 00:00:13,664
differently.

6
00:00:14,386 --> 00:00:17,003
We can create and work with Sets like this

7
00:00:17,132 --> 00:00:17,854
in JavaScript.

8
00:00:18,497 --> 00:00:21,130
We don't have such a shortcut syntax like

9
00:00:21,130 --> 00:00:22,720
with the square brackets for arrays.

10
00:00:23,073 --> 00:00:25,000
Instead, we have to use the Set constructor

11
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:25,417
function.

12
00:00:25,963 --> 00:00:28,528
And then on the created object, we can use

13
00:00:28,528 --> 00:00:31,191
the add method to add items to the Set.

14
00:00:31,720 --> 00:00:33,532
Now you already see in this example, there's

15
00:00:33,660 --> 00:00:36,290
one important thing about Sets. Duplicate

16
00:00:36,371 --> 00:00:38,744
items are not allowed. You won't get an

17
00:00:39,017 --> 00:00:40,989
error if you try to add one, but it also

18
00:00:41,038 --> 00:00:43,170
won't be added a second time or a third

19
00:00:43,203 --> 00:00:44,469
time. It's just added once.

20
00:00:45,752 --> 00:00:47,597
Now what else is interesting about Sets?

21
00:00:48,158 --> 00:00:51,109
The insertion order, unlike for Arrays, is

22
00:00:51,237 --> 00:00:54,830
not stored. So you can't rely on the order

23
00:00:54,830 --> 00:00:57,604
being kept. Therefore, of course, you can't

24
00:00:57,636 --> 00:00:59,945
access elements with index, but instead

25
00:00:59,945 --> 00:01:02,030
you'll have a method for getting access to

26
00:01:02,030 --> 00:01:02,463
an element.

27
00:01:03,185 --> 00:01:06,280
Sets, like arrays, are iterable though, so

28
00:01:06,280 --> 00:01:08,749
you can use the for-of loop there, but the

29
00:01:08,845 --> 00:01:11,058
order, of course, could be different for

30
00:01:11,267 --> 00:01:13,255
different loops, so the order is not

31
00:01:13,255 --> 00:01:14,875
guaranteed. That's something to keep in

32
00:01:14,875 --> 00:01:15,164
mind.

33
00:01:16,078 --> 00:01:18,162
And the size and length is also adjusted

34
00:01:18,162 --> 00:01:20,616
dynamically, so just like with arrays, you

35
00:01:20,632 --> 00:01:21,899
don't have to worry about that.

36
00:01:22,933 --> 00:01:25,199
Now, as I mentioned, duplicate values are

37
00:01:25,263 --> 00:01:28,686
not allowed. So in a Set, you'll always only

38
00:01:28,782 --> 00:01:30,373
have unique values.

39
00:01:31,112 --> 00:01:33,060
And there's one other big difference

40
00:01:33,060 --> 00:01:34,398
compared to Arrays.

41
00:01:35,300 --> 00:01:38,813
Deletion and finding elements is more

42
00:01:38,862 --> 00:01:41,272
trivial and faster than with Arrays.

43
00:01:43,700 --> 00:01:45,958
The simple reason for that is that the order

44
00:01:46,007 --> 00:01:49,115
does not matter. Sets can internally be

45
00:01:49,115 --> 00:01:50,446
managed differently.

46
00:01:51,120 --> 00:01:53,077
For arrays, you always have to go through

47
00:01:53,205 --> 00:01:56,430
all elements and so on. Now, sets can simply

48
00:01:56,430 --> 00:01:58,547
store the data more efficiently internally

49
00:01:58,660 --> 00:02:01,371
because the position of a value does not

50
00:02:01,371 --> 00:02:03,905
matter. So there's no need to go through all

51
00:02:04,114 --> 00:02:06,119
values. It can instead use different

52
00:02:06,119 --> 00:02:08,445
techniques for quickly finding a value. The

53
00:02:08,445 --> 00:02:10,771
same for deleting. If you delete an element

54
00:02:10,771 --> 00:02:13,370
from a set, it doesn't have to move all

55
00:02:13,643 --> 00:02:16,000
other elements. Because elements didn't have

56
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:18,116
a position in the first place. So there is

57
00:02:18,164 --> 00:02:20,761
no need to move anything just because

58
00:02:20,793 --> 00:02:21,963
something was deleted.

59
00:02:22,636 --> 00:02:24,768
Now let's have a look at Sets in code as

60
00:02:24,865 --> 00:02:24,993
well.

61
